From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RTL8197F/RD05 port <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 18:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: rtl8197f/rtl8367d: document mainstream offload replacement

The Realtek SDK exposes swconfig, private IOCTLs, FastPath/HWNAT and ACL table
programming through non-upstream ABIs.  Keep the kernel port aligned with
standard Linux interfaces: DSA/bridge VLANs, ethtool diagnostics, nftables
flowtables and tc flower.  The driver implements Linux 6.6 ndo_setup_tc()/flow_block callback binding so
OpenWrt can translate SDK private IOCTL/FastPath/ACL requests through standard
tc/nft hooks.  Unsupported hardware table encodings fail explicitly and fall
back to software instead of creating a private ABI.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/Kconfig
@@ -41,6 +41,24 @@ config RTL8197F_RTKNET
 	  This driver does not import Realtek's legacy NAT/fastpath/swconfig stack.
 	  It still requires board-level validation of descriptor address format,
 	  port-mask semantics and external switch wiring.
+
+config RTL8197F_RTKNET_MAINSTREAM_OFFLOADS
+	bool "RTL8197F mainstream offload control-plane documentation"
+	depends on RTL8197F_RTKNET
+	default y if RTL8197F_RTKNET
+	help
+	  The Realtek RTL8197F SDK provided swconfig, private IOCTLs, FastPath/HWNAT
+	  and ACL control paths.  Those are intentionally not reintroduced as kernel
+	  ABIs.  OpenWrt 24.10 should use:
+
+	    - DSA and bridge VLANs instead of swconfig;
+	    - ethtool and, where appropriate, devlink/debugfs for diagnostics;
+	    - nftables flowtables for software fastpath;
+	    - tc flower for switch ACL/offload requests;
+	    - Linux flowtable offload callbacks for future rtl865x HWNAT.
+
+	  Selecting this symbol documents that the compatibility layer is expected to
+	  live above standard Linux APIs rather than through Realtek private hooks.
 
 config SUNGEM_PHY
 	tristate
